# Git amend on explicit order

When the user **explicitly orders** an amend — including date-only rewrites, message fixes, or including hook-touched files — the agent **must** run `git commit --amend` as requested, even if HEAD was **not** created by the agent in this conversation.

This **overrides** the default “HEAD must be agent-created in this chat” amend gate.

## Still required

- Prefer `--no-edit` for date-only amends
- Do **not** amend a commit that is already on the remote unless the user explicitly accepts a history rewrite (and any needed force-push); warn if pushed
- Never use `git reset` to achieve an amend (see `no-git-reset`)
- Never skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it
- Never add Co-authored-by / AI trailers (see `no-commit-co-authors`)

## Date-only amend

Use the datetime the user gave (ISO 8601 with offset when possible):

```bash
GIT_COMMITTER_DATE="<datetime>" git commit --amend --no-edit --date "<datetime>"
```
